      "part_type": "Hadith",
      "path": "/books/al-kafi:6:4:1:7",
      "text": [
        " سَأَلْتُ أَبَا عَبْدِ اللَّهِ ( عليه السلام ) عَنْ رَجُلٍ أَرْسَلَ كَلْبَهُ فَأَدْرَكَهُ وَ قَدْ قَتَلَ قَالَ كُلْ وَ إِنْ أَكَلَ ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "Ahmad Bin Muhammad, from Muhassan Bin Ahmad, from Yunus Bin Yaqoub who said, ",
          "‘I asked Abu Abdullah<sup>asws</sup> about a man who sent his dog (for hunting). So when he came to it, and it had killed it’. He<sup>asws</sup> said: ‘Eat, and even if it has eaten (from it)’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "7. Ahmad ibn Muhammad has narrated from Muhsin ibn Ahmad from Yunus ibn Ya’qub who has said the following: “I once asked abu ‘Abd Allah, ‘Alayhi al-Salam, about the case of a man who sends his dog and he arrives at the site when the dog has killed the prey. He (the Imam) said, ‘You can use it for food even if the dog has eaten thereof.’” "
        ]
      }
    },
